// With Program.onUncaughtError set, it takes the error that ends a thread, on that thread as it
// ends, in place of the report; the exit code is the program's own (8.7a).
Program.onUncaughtError = { error -> print("handled:", error.message, "on", Thread.currentThread().name) }
val worker = Thread("unlucky") { throw RuntimeException("worker gave up") }
worker.start()
worker.join()                                                // expect: handled: worker gave up on unlucky
print("and the program goes on")                             // expect: and the program goes on
